   8 // scanCacheVersion marks a file whose entries are grouped by configuration
   9 // context. Version 0 is the shape that predates contexts: a bare key → entry
  10 // map, which is what `Contexts == nil` after a successful unmarshal means.
  11 const scanCacheVersion = 1
  12 
  13 // scanCacheFile is the on-disk shape of the workspace scan cache, and of the
  14 // image scan cache as it was written between the arrival of contexts and §3.39.
  15 //
  16 // A workspace path is reached through `workspaces_dir`, which is per context, so
  17 // two contexts holding the same path may legitimately mean different work — one
  18 // flat namespace made them share results. An image key is a local Docker
  19 // reference and answers for the machine, which is why that cache is flat again;
  20 // the image side still reads this shape to fold it back (readImageScanCacheFile).
  21 type scanCacheFile[T any] struct {
  22     Version  int                     `json:"version"`
  23     Contexts map[string]map[string]T `json:"contexts"`
  24 }
  25 
  26 // readScanCacheFile loads every context's entries, upgrading the file in place
  27 // when it predates contexts. parseScanCacheFile is the same read without the
  28 // upgrade.
  29 //
  30 // The upgrade is written back immediately rather than left until the first Set.
  31 // Deferring it would let every context that opens the file claim the legacy
  32 // entries in turn, so what the user saw would depend on which context happened
  33 // to write first. Writing once, on the first open, makes the owner the context
  34 // that was current at upgrade time and nothing else.
  35 func readScanCacheFile[T any](path, context string) (map[string]map[string]T, error) {
  36     contexts, legacy, err := parseScanCacheFile[T](path)
  37     if err != nil {
  38         return nil, err
  39     }
  40     if len(legacy) == 0 {
  41         return contexts, nil
  42     }
  43 
  44     contexts[context] = legacy
  45     if err := writeScanCacheFile(path, contexts); err != nil {
  46         return nil, err
  47     }
  48     return contexts, nil
  49 }
  50 
  51 // parseScanCacheFile reads the file and upgrades nothing.
  52 //
  53 // It returns the per-context entries, and *separately* the entries of a legacy
  54 // pre-context file — which belong to no context yet. Deciding whose they are is
  55 // a write, and this function does not make it: that is the whole reason it
  56 // exists beside readScanCacheFile, which does.
  57 //
  58 // The read-only MCP server is what needs the distinction (§3.38). A server
  59 // opened on context X would otherwise claim for X entries nobody attributed to
  60 // it — a read path that writes, and decides. It serves them and leaves the
  61 // decision to the TUI, where somebody is present to see it.
  62 //
  63 // A legacy file is a bare key → entry map. Unmarshalled into the struct it
  64 // leaves Version at 0 and Contexts nil — no field matches — which identifies it
  65 // without having to guess from the data.
  66 //
  67 // A file that cannot be read is empty, not an error: that is a cache which does
  68 // not exist yet.
  69 func parseScanCacheFile[T any](path string) (contexts map[string]map[string]T, legacy map[string]T, err error) {
  70     data, readErr := os.ReadFile(path)
  71     if readErr != nil {
  72         return map[string]map[string]T{}, nil, nil
  73     }
  74 
  75     var file scanCacheFile[T]
  76     if err := json.Unmarshal(data, &file); err == nil && file.Contexts != nil {
  77         return file.Contexts, nil, nil
  78     }
  79 
  80     var flat map[string]T
  81     if err := json.Unmarshal(data, &flat); err != nil {
  82         return nil, nil, err
  83     }
  84     if len(flat) == 0 {
  85         return map[string]map[string]T{}, nil, nil
  86     }
  87     return map[string]map[string]T{}, flat, nil
  88 }
  89 
  90 // writeScanCacheFile persists every context, not just the one that changed —
  91 // the caller holds them all, and dropping the others would make a write from
  92 // one context erase the rest.
  93 func writeScanCacheFile[T any](path string, contexts map[string]map[string]T) error {
  94     data, err := json.MarshalIndent(scanCacheFile[T]{
  95         Version:  scanCacheVersion,
  96         Contexts: contexts,
  97     }, "", "  ")
  98     if err != nil {
  99         return err
 100     }
 101     return os.WriteFile(path, data, 0600)
 102 }
